{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.HomologicalShellCondensation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.HomologicalShellCondensation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Common.MagicNumbers"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_diagonal_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_diagonal_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L109-L119","doc":"Conditional theorem: at a saturated level, every diagonal\nentry `E_∞^{p, p}` for `p ≥ 1` is also trivial — the BB\nspectral sequence collapses on the entire upper-triangular\nregion above the `q = 0` line, not just the strictly off-\ndiagonal part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_add_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_add_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L99-L107","doc":"Conditional corollary: at a saturated level, every additive\noperation in the strict-positive part of `E_∞` is trivial.\n`x + y = 0` for any `x, y` in the strict-positive page. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L88-L97","doc":"Conditional theorem: the strict-positive part of the `E_∞`\npage contains exactly one element (the zero of the additive\ngroup), at a saturated level. Combines `Subsingleton` with\nthe existence of `EInftyZero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L78-L86","doc":"Conditional theorem: at a saturated level, the strict-positive\npart of the `E_∞` page is a singleton (the zero subgroup). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_collapse_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.strict_positive_collapse_unique","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L67-L76","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the homological-condensation\nconjecture, every two elements of the strict-positive part of\n`E_∞` at a saturated level are equal (since they are both\nzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.collapse","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The asserted vanishing: every entry above the `E_2` line is\nthe zero element of its group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.saturated","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Precondition: `n` is saturated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.toBBSpectralSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture.toBBSpectralSequence","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L59-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.HomologicalConjecture","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L52-L65","doc":"The conjecture, encoded as a class.\n\nA `HomologicalConjecture n` instance asserts that the strict-\npositive part of the `E_∞` page vanishes at the saturated level\n`n`. The unproved input is the existence of the instance;\ndownstream conditional theorems are then fully verified. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:homological-shell-condensation","label":"prop:homological-shell-condensation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.EInftyZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.EInftyZero","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L48-L48","doc":"A canonical zero element to compare against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.EInftyAddGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.EInftyAddGroup","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Each entry is a commutative additive group (so \"vanishing\"\nmeans \"trivial\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.EInfty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.EInfty","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The `E_∞` page entries, abstracted as a function of the\nbigrading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.BBSpectralSequence","kind":"class","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L32-L48","doc":"The data of a Białynicki-Birula bigraded `E_∞` page at level\n`n`. The conjecture below asks whether this page vanishes above\nthe `E_2` line.\n\nConcretely the QOU substrate instantiates `EInfty p q` as\n`H^q(gr_F^p A_n)` where `A_n` is the descent-graded brane-tower\nalgebra and `F` is the BB-filtration induced by the descent\ninvolution `τ̂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.Saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.Saturated","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellCondensation.magicSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellCondensation.magicSet","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/homological-shell-condensation.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0}]}